@namespace PgmStudio.Client.Components

@* The four pictures of a building, shown wherever one is being composed — a room style, a roof, a storey, a
   porch. One component because the four views are the building rather than the editor: an isometric of what it
   looks like, a plan of what the roof does, a section through the course stack, and a cutaway of one plane at
   the scale of the pieces in it. Every one is stamped by the real HouseStamper and read back out of the world,
   so none can promise a building the export would not put down.

   Together they are the isometric over a row of the three cuts, because the isometric is what the building
   looks like and the cuts are how it is made — two questions, not four pictures. Any one of them can be asked
   for alone, which is the only way to read a cut at the size the stage can give it.

   A library *card* deliberately carries only the section: an isometric runs tens of kilobytes, which is
   nothing once and megabytes in a grid. *@

@if (Preview is not null)
{
  @if (Shows(Iso))
  {
    <figure class="house-views__iso">@((MarkupString)Preview.Iso)</figure>
  }
  @if (Shows(Plan) || Shows(Section) || Shows(Cutaway))
  {
    <div class="house-views__cuts">
      @if (Shows(Plan)) { <figure class="house-views__cut">@((MarkupString)Preview.Plan)</figure> }
      @if (Shows(Section)) { <figure class="house-views__cut">@((MarkupString)Preview.Section)</figure> }
      @if (Shows(Cutaway)) { <figure class="house-views__cut">@((MarkupString)Preview.Cutaway)</figure> }
    </div>
  }
}
